		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: AAA Titles using Bullet ?]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=11971#p11971"><![CDATA[
In most cases, a non-disclosure agreement prevents sharing this information. There are some AAA games released by Sony Computer Entertainment, Disney and Rockstar and others, next to smaller releases such as <a href="http://www.metacritic.com/games/platforms/ps3/highvelocitybowling" class="postlink">High Velocity Bowling</a> for PLAYSTATION 3.<br><br>As an exception, we are allowed to mention that some parts of Bullet have been co-developed and optimized with Rockstar and merged into their Rage game engine, used on XBox 360, PC and PLAYSTATION 3 in <a href="http://www.metacritic.com/games/platforms/ps3/midnightclublosangeles" class="postlink">Midnight Club: Los Angeles</a> and <a href="http://www.metacritic.com/games/platforms/ps3/grandtheftauto4" class="postlink">Grand Theft Auto 4</a>.<br><br>Hope this helps,<br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Mon Jan 05, 2009 7:32 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
